Eva: opened PR to add a compact "cursor checkpoint" pattern + dedupe note to streaming pagination snippets for py/ts/go. shows checkpoint token storage and non-blocking resume. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/824
Mira: nice, that checkpoint pattern will help users with intermittent reconnects. can we keep examples minimal but show how to dedupe tokens when pages partially overlap?
Harry: quick thought: include a tiny python example that persists only the latest resume_token and a dedupe set keyed by token.id. avoids storing long histories.
Eva: added this python snippet:
```python
# python: checkpoint + lightweight dedupe
seen = set()
async for page in client.responses.stream_paginate(prompt, cursor=None):
    for tok in page.tokens:
        if tok.id in seen:
            continue
        process(tok)
        seen.add(tok.id)
    # persist checkpoint for quick resume
    last_checkpoint = page.resume_token
    await kv.store("resume_token", last_checkpoint)
    if page.had_transient_error:
        await retry_with_jitter(lambda: client.responses.resume(last_checkpoint))
```
Mira: looks good. add a one-liner about token.id not being guaranteed across model versions. suggest using (id,offset) tuple for long-term dedupe.
Harry: done. TS examples: can we show both generator (`for await`) and an EventEmitter style that emits 'page' events? some frontend integrations expect evented APIs.
Eva: added both. EventEmitter variant:
```ts
// ts: event emitter style
const emitter = client.responses.streamPaginateEmitter({ prompt })
emitter.on('page', (page) => {
  page.tokens.forEach(t => { if (!seenSet.has(t.id)) { handle(t); seenSet.add(t.id) } })
})
emitter.on('error', async (err) => {
  if (err.type === 'TransientError') await retryWithJitter(() => client.responses.resume(err.cursor))
})
```
Owen: CI flagged a gofmt diff and a comment about context cancellation in my go example. I'll adjust to use a cancelable ctx and a channel consumer pattern.
Eva: go example should show channel consumption + dedupe map and a small note to check rate-limit headers before aggressive retries.
Owen: pushed fix. go snippet now:
```go
// go: channel consumer + checkpoint
ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
defer cancel()
seen := map[string]bool{}
for page := range client.Responses.StreamPaginate(ctx, req) {
    for _, tok := range page.Tokens {
        if seen[tok.ID] { continue }
        handle(tok)
        seen[tok.ID] = true
    }
    // store last checkpoint
    _ = kv.Store(ctx, "resume_token", page.ResumeToken)
    if page.TransientError {
        err := retryWithJitter(func() error { return client.Responses.Resume(ctx, page.ResumeToken) })
        if err != nil { log.Printf("resume failed: %v", err) }
    }
}
```
Harry: tiny doc nit: recommend a TTL-based checkpoint expiry note and call out that resume tokens may be short-lived behind load-balancers.
Mira: agree. also add migration note recommending checkpoint over naive offsets for sharded backends. Put a small CHANGELOG line and backport to release/v1.9 as docs-only.
Eva: added migration paragraph and CHANGELOG entry. also added a short link to the internal eval that found partial overlap cases.
link-bot: link-checker: 5/5 links validated. docs-lint: warn long-line in ts example (Eva to wrap).
Eva: wrapped long line, pushed.
ci-bot: CI green after gofmt and wrap fixes. ready for final review.
Mira: LGTM, left one wording nit about "checkpoint" vs "resume_token" naming. unified to "resume_token" in migration text. approving now.
Eva: merging and will post a short summary to #integrations and add an examples/streaming/checkpoint sample as follow-up. thanks all :shipit:
Harry: nice work!
